This states the position that already applied. Source with no licence file is
all rights reserved by default — the same terms — but a default is silence,
and silence is indistinguishable from an oversight to anyone reading the
repository, including a diligence team.

Where this estate intends the opposite it says so and ships the text: the
specification and the published clients are Apache-2.0 so anyone may embed
them, and the hosted services are AGPL-3.0-only so a hosted fork must publish
its changes. The choice is recorded once, for every repository, in
tools/estate-licences.mjs in flashyos — not decided here.

